  <h2>If the Osmo Pocket only charges</h2>
  <p>Check that the cable carries data and USB Mode is selected on the camera. If Android shows a USB notification, open it to view the connected storage. You should be able to browse the camera’s <code>DCIM</code> folder.</p>
  <p><a href="https://www.dji.com/osmo-pocket-4p/faq">DJI Osmo Pocket 4P FAQ</a></p>

  <h2>Does this work with the Osmo Pocket 3 or Pocket 4?</h2>
  <p>DJI documents OTG transfer for the Osmo Pocket 3 and Pocket 4. Hikkonuki has been tested with the Pocket 4P. Compatibility with the Pocket 3 and Pocket 4 is unverified. To try either model, first check whether Android’s folder picker can open the camera’s <code>DCIM</code> folder.</p>
  <p><a href="https://repair.dji.com/help/content?customId=01700007307&amp;documentType=&amp;lang=en&amp;paperDocType=ARTICLE&amp;re=US&amp;spaceId=17">DJI’s guide to USB OTG on Android</a></p>
</CameraGuide>
